{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":13642,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"YbeY is a single strand-specific metallo-endoribonuclease involved in late-stage 70S ribosome quality control and in maturation of the 3' terminus of the 16S rRNA. It acts together with the RNase R to eliminate defective 70S ribosomes, but not properly maturated 70S ribosomes or individual subunits, by a process mediated specifically by the 30S ribosomal subunit. It is involved in the processing of 16S, 23S and 5S rRNAs, with a particularly strong effect on maturation at both the 5'-and 3'-ends of 16S rRNA as well as maturation of the 5'-end of 23S and 5S rRNAs [[cite:PUB00064743],[cite:PUB00064742],[cite:PUB00096939]]. The crystal structure of the protein from Aquifex aeolicus showed an overall fold consisting of one central alpha-helix surrounded by a four-stranded beta-sheet and four other alpha-helices [[cite:PUB00027806]].","domain_architectures":53,"interpro_id":"IPR002036","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":20283,"name":"Endoribonuclease YbeY","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF02130","proteins":20178,"proteomes":19123,"short_name":"YbeY","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF02130","structures":5,"taxa":29306,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-direct-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","history":[{"action":"CREATE","agent":"Codex","curator":"Codex","description":"Inspected Jacob 2013 main methods and Figures 1 and 3; resolved historical P77385 demerger to E. coli P0A898. Added two scope