.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/P0A898/entry/pfam/PF02130/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"In the separately prepared kasugamycin-treated-cell substrate, joint enzyme addition causes rRNA-band loss while either enzyme alone and mutant-YbeY plus RNase R do not.","object":"kasugamycin-70s-rrna","predicate":"degrades","subject":"joint-ybey-rnaser","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"E. coli YbeY maps from historical P77385 to UniProtKB:P0A898, b0659/JW0656, reference sequence version 1, PF02130 at 21-144 of 155 residues. The graph concerns the intact-protein preparation in conjunction with RNase R, not a sufficient isolated PF02130 domain.","graph_id":"ecoli-ybey-rnaser-defective-70s","limitations":"Neither enzyme alone nor H114A/H124A YbeY plus RNase R gives the adopted rRNA-band-loss endpoint. Matched wild-type 70S and 30S controls resist treatment. Ordered initiation and exonucleolytic microsteps remain proposed, and gel band loss does not demonstrate degradation of ribosomal proteins. Purification tag and full construct details remain unresolved; in vivo quality-control flux and polysome endpoints are not adopted here.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:P0A898"],"label":"Joint purified YbeY and RNase R treatment","node_id":"joint-ybey-rnaser","node_type":"ACTIVITY"},{"label":"rRNA in 70S preparations from MC4100 delta-ybeY","node_id":"deletion-70s-rrna","node_type":"STATE"},{"label":"rRNA in 70S preparations from kasugamycin-treated MC4100","node_id":"kasugamycin-70s-rrna","node_type":"STATE"}],"scope":"In vitro treatment of separate 70S preparations from E. coli MC4100 delta-ybeY and kasugamycin-treated MC4100; the two substrate contexts are distinct comparisons within Figure 3, not independent replications.","scope_status":"MECHANISTIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:83333","title":"Joint YbeY and RNase R treatment degrades rRNA in defective 70S preparations"}],"characterization_status":"UNSCORED","counters":{"alphafold_models":13642,"domain_architect